<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Freshli uses your camera to scan barcodes, scan receipts, and identify fresh ingredients with Freshli Vision. If you enable the optional Gaze-Adaptive UI accessibility feature in Settings, Freshli also uses the TrueDepth camera via ARKit face tracking purely on-device to compute where you are looking on screen — no face data is ever stored, transmitted, or shared.</string>
	<key>NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Freshli accesses your photos to add images to pantry items and community listings.</string>
	<key>NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Freshli saves shared recipe images and impact cards to your photo library.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Freshli uses your location to show nearby community food listings and set pickup locations.</string>
	<key>NSFaceIDUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Freshli uses Face ID to confirm you're the account owner when you stake a Trust Badge on a community listing or claim. Your face data never leaves the device — Apple's Face ID handles authentication entirely on-device.</string>
	<key>NSMotionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Freshli uses gyroscope readings to make the Liquid Glass surfaces catch the light as you tilt your device — the same way real glass would. Motion data is read only while the app is open, never sent off-device, and never stored.</string>
	<key>NSCalendarsFullAccessUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Freshli can add expiry dates to your Calendar so you see what needs using on your daily agenda. This is optional — you'll be asked the first time you turn it on in Settings.</string>
	<key>NSRemindersFullAccessUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Freshli can create Reminders for items expiring soon so you get a Lock Screen nudge a day before. This is optional — you'll be asked the first time you turn it on in Settings.</string>
	<key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
	<false/>
	<!--
	  Custom URL scheme for App Store In-App Event deep links.

	  Required so iOS routes `freshli://events/<slug>` URLs to this app.
	  Each App Store In-App Event configured in App Store Connect uses
	  one of these slugs as its Event Deep Link:

	    freshli://events/spring-pantry-reset
	    freshli://events/world-environment-day
	    freshli://events/plastic-free-july
	    freshli://events/bbq-saver
	    freshli://events/lunch-lab
	    freshli://events/world-food-day
	    freshli://events/holiday-pantry-hero

	  Routing is handled by `URLRouterService` (Services/UI/URLRouterService.swift),
	  which receives the URL via `.onOpenURL` in FreshliApp.swift.

	  Universal Links (https://freshli.app/events/<slug>) resolve to the same
	  routes — see the Associated Domains entitlement and the AASA file.
	-->
	<key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
			<string>Editor</string>
			<key>CFBundleURLName</key>
			<string>everwise.interactive.Freshli</string>
			<key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
			<array>
				<string>freshli</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
